  "description": "There are 31 elementary, unified and high school districts in Santa Clara County.  Elementary school districts (N=20) include Alum Rock, Berryessa, Cambrian, Campbell, Cupertino, Evergreen, Franklin-McKinley, Lakeside, Loma Prieta, Los Altos, Los Gatos, Luther Burbank, Moreland, Mount Pleasant, Mountain View-Whisman, Oak Grove, Orchard, Saratoga, Sunnyvale, and Union.  Unified school districts (N=6) include Gilroy, Milpitas, Morgan Hill, Palo Alto, San Jose, and Santa Clara.  High school districts (N=5) include Campbell, East Side, Fremont, Los Gatos-Saratoga, and Mountain View-Los Altos.  Elementary school district boundaries are nested within high school districts.<div><br /><\/div><div><span style='font-family:&quot;Avenir Next W01&quot;, &quot;Avenir Next W00&quot;, &quot;Avenir Next&quot;, Avenir, &quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;, sans-serif; font-size:16px;'>Data last updated: Feb 2021<\/span><\/div>",
